      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into doses (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
